    <statement><p>Find the eigenvalues <m>\lambda_1 \lt  \lambda_2 \lt  \lambda_3</m> and corresponding eigenvectors of the matrix
<me>A = \left[\begin{array}{ccc}
-4 \amp 20 \amp 44\cr
0 \amp 0 \amp -4\cr
0 \amp 0 \amp 4
\end{array}\right].</me></p>
<p>The eigenvalue
<m>\lambda_1 =</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/> corresponds to the eigenvector <fillin rows="3"/>.</p>
<p>The eigenvalue
<m>\lambda_2 =</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/> corresponds to the eigenvector <fillin rows="3"/>.</p>
<p>The eigenvalue
<m>\lambda_3 =</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0005"/> corresponds to the eigenvector <fillin rows="3"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
